 in Rio Grande County.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding along the Rio Grande near Monte Vista is forecasted\nto begin by early afternoon on Monday.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...The Rio Grande continues to rise due to upstream flooding\nthrough Del Norte and South Fork. Extensive inundation of low-lying\nareas adjacent to the river is expected. Inundation of low spots\nalong Highway 285, some homes, and other structures may be possible\nfor areas south of the river. Expect many areas of slow moving or\nstanding water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1251 PM MST, Upstream stream gauges on the Rio Grande and\nSouth Fork Rio Grande indicate that flooding is occurring.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMonte Vista.\n- http://water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-02T21:30:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da4d217834c7088518767dad11bd998f6f765b61.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da4d217834c7088518767dad11bd998f6f765b61.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 7:19AM MST until November 3 at 7:34PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte...Moderate\nflooding is forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 7.0 feet, Moderate Flood. Water flows into farm\nproperties and homes west of Del Norte. Serious lowland and meadow\nflooding occurs.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:01 AM MST Monday the stage was 6.6 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 7:01 AM MST Monday was 6.6 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 7.0 feet\nlate this afternoon. It will then fall below flood stage tomorrow\nmorning.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 6.8\nfeet on 10/05/1911.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-03T19:34:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e9053015039ef7b205c67b91b64c8c59ba59a9c9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e9053015039ef7b205c67b91b64c8c59ba59a9c9.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T23:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 022320 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 420 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Strong north winds and showers/isolated t-storms on the plains into this evening, perhaps some snow showers along the Palmer Divide overnight. - Generally dry and breezy on Tue, strongest winds early in the day on the plains. - Weak trough will bring scattered show","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T08:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 020809 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 109 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-030815- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosqu","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T21:27:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... No critical fire weather conditions are expected over the next several days. Showers will gradually come to an end this evening, 